{"slug":"balanced-letter-splits","title":"Splits With Equally Many Different Letters","topic":"hashing","difficulty":"medium","order":272,"tags":["hashing","hash-set","prefix","strings"],"timeLimitMs":2000,"concept":{"title":"Distinct letters of every prefix and every suffix","body":["A **split** cuts the word into a non-empty left part and a non-empty right part. You want to count the splits where both parts contain the **same number of different letters**. Checking each split from scratch costs `O(n)` each, `O(n^2)` in total. Instead precompute two arrays: `pre[i]` = number of different letters in the first `i` letters, and `suf[i]` = number of different letters in the letters from position `i` to the end. Each is built with one pass and a set.",{"code":"seen = set(); pre = [0] * (n + 1)\nfor i, ch in enumerate(s):\n    seen.add(ch)\n    pre[i + 1] = len(seen)\n# suf is built the same way from the right\ncount = sum(1 for i in range(1, n) if pre[i] == suf[i])"},"The number of different letters of a prefix can only grow, so a set that is never cleared gives all prefix values in one pass. The suffixes are processed from the right end in the same way."]},"statement":["Cut a word into two non-empty parts (the first `i` letters and the rest, for `i` from 1 to length - 1). Count the cuts for which both parts contain the same number of different letters."],"inputFormat":["A single word of lowercase letters."],"outputFormat":["Print the number of cuts."],"constraints":["1 <= length <= 20000"],"examples":[{"input":"aacaba\n","output":"2\n","note":"The cuts aac|aba and aaca|ba have 2 different letters on each side: two good cuts."}],"hints":["Build an array with the number of different letters of every prefix.","Build an array with the same for every suffix.","Count the cut positions where both values are equal."],"starter":{"python":"s = input().strip()\n\n# Your code here\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\n#include <unordered_set>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    string s;\n    cin >> s;\n\n    // Your code here\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        String s = sc.next();\n\n        // Your code here\n    }\n}\n"},"solution":{"explanation":["Two sets built from the left and from the right give the number of different letters of every prefix and suffix; a cut is counted when the two values agree."],"complexity":"Time O(n) on average, space O(n).","code":{"python":"s = input().strip()\n\nn = len(s)\npre = [0] * (n + 1)\nsuf = [0] * (n + 1)\nseen = set()\nfor i in range(n):\n    seen.add(s[i])\n    pre[i + 1] = len(seen)\nseen = set()\nfor i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n    seen.add(s[i])\n    suf[i] = len(seen)\nprint(sum(1 for i in range(1, n) if pre[i] == suf[i]))\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\n#include <unordered_set>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    string s;\n    cin >> s;\n\n    int n = s.size();\n    vector<int> pre(n + 1, 0), suf(n + 1, 0);\n    unordered_set<char> seen;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        seen.insert(s[i]);\n        pre[i + 1] = seen.size();\n    }\n    seen.clear();\n    for (int i = n - 1; i >= 0; i--) {\n        seen.insert(s[i]);\n        suf[i] = seen.size();\n    }\n    int count = 0;\n    for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {\n        if (pre[i] == suf[i]) count++;\n    }\n    cout << count << \"\\n\";\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        String s = sc.next();\n\n        int n = s.length();\n        int[] pre = new int[n + 1], suf = new int[n + 1];\n        Set<Character> seen = new HashSet<>();\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            seen.add(s.charAt(i));\n            pre[i + 1] = seen.size();\n        }\n        seen.clear();\n        for (int i = n - 1; i >= 0; i--) {\n            seen.add(s.charAt(i));\n            suf[i] = seen.size();\n        }\n        int count = 0;\n        for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {\n            if (pre[i] == suf[i]) count++;\n        }\n        System.out.println(count);\n    }\n}\n"}},"tests":[{"input":"aacaba\n","output":"2\n"},{"input":"a\n","output":"0\n"},{"input":"ab\n","output":"1\n"},{"input":"aaaa\n","output":"3\n"},{"input":"abcd\n","output":"1\n"},{"input":"abab\n","output":"1\n"},{"input":"aabacaaaaaaacbcbbbbcbbbabacbab\n","output":"22\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"371\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"2738\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"5996\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"4997\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"4961\n"}]}